I'm mapping out a simplified architecture for an ID Generator service, utilizing a stateful set with stable pod ordinals as node IDs, operating behind a Layer 4/Layer 7 load balancer. I plan to avoid the need for a separate registry service or etcd, using a ConfigMap for configuration management. Multi-region routing will depend on clients having a list of endpoints, with simple DNS CNAMEs for failover. While considering the option of generating IDs within each app service, I realize node ID uniqueness could complicate things. Therefore, it seems best to keep a single ID generation service, capable of handling 200k requests per second.
